Keeps the iOS native tab view mounted when a trigger's `hidden` flips (task 0071, decision 5).

expo-router keys NativeTabsView on the visible triggers' route keys, so showing or hiding a
trigger remounts every tab: their stacks, scroll positions and state. The key came with
https://github.com/expo/expo/pull/42329 ("react-native-screens does not support dynamic changes
to tab visibility"). On iOS, react-native-screens 4.26.2 inserts and removes the tab in place,
so the patch drops the key there; Android keeps it, since its tabs host still does not remove a
screen natively (https://github.com/software-mansion/react-native-screens/pull/4812).

Drop this patch when expo-router stops keying the tab view on iOS. Applied by postinstall
(patch-package --error-on-fail --error-on-warn), so an expo-router upgrade fails the install
until the patch is regenerated or removed; see mobile/README.md.

